# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# All variables are read at RUNTIME via `$env/dynamic/public` (never the static
# `$env/static/*` modules), so the same build is portable across environments.
# Copy this file to `.env` for local development.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Base URL (host only) of the backend REST API — no version segment here.
# Each endpoint carries its own version inline (e.g. /v1/auth/login), so a single
# endpoint can move to /v2 independently.
# Leave EMPTY while the backend does not exist yet: the app then runs in dev mode
# (dashboard reachable without login). Filling it in enables the real auth guard.
# Example: http://localhost:8080
PUBLIC_BASE_API_URL=
